ctlsock: a letterboxed raster has its own clamp box — MAME_CTL_SCREEN WxH+X+Y

Applies AFTER mame-ctlsock-count-carry.patch (same file, last of the chain).

THE BUG, measured on fmtowns (MAME fmtownsftv, Towns OS V2.1 L51, 2026-09-13).
The station publishes a 1024x768 surface, but the FM Towns raster inside that
shm frame occupies only cols 61..991 and rows 48..749 — 931x702, letterboxed,
everything outside it black. The guest's own pointer cannot leave that box:
slamming the mouse into the top-left clamp parks the cursor sprite at exactly
(61,48), and no number of further negative counts moves it.

The module did not know. clamp_px_x/y clamped the belief to [0, m_surf_w-1],
the open-loop homing slam anchored the belief at (0,0), and movea_target()
accepted any target on the published surface. So a five-target proof that
aims at the corners of the SURFACE — (20,20), (1000,20), (20,740), (1000,740)
— measured errors of 42-51 px that no amount of pacing or gain correction
could move, because the guest was at its clamp and the belief was 41 px to
the left and 28 px above it. Worse, an open loop has only its belief: the
first corner target poisons every later one. The centre target, visited after
two corners, missed by 103 px.

	target        landed     err     what it actually was
	(20,20)      (61,48)      50     the raster's top-left clamp
	(1000,20)    (991,70)     51     the raster's right clamp
	(20,740)     (61,749)     42     the raster's left/bottom clamp
	(1000,740)   (991,746)    11     the raster's bottom-right clamp
	(512,384)    (435,315)   103     inherited border debt + a 9% gain error

Lap two was bit-identical to lap one, which is the signature of a clamp, not
of jitter.

THE FIX. MAME_CTL_SCREEN gains an optional X-geometry tail: WxH+X+Y, where
+X+Y is the raster's origin inside the published surface (fmtowns:
931x702+61+48). clamp_px_x/y then clamp to [X, X+W-1] and [Y, Y+H-1];
movea_target() clamps its target through the same two functions instead of
its own open-coded 0-based pair; and every site that anchors the belief at
the "top-left clamp" after a homing slam — the restore reseed, drain_move()'s
release of the held first target, and the MAME_CTL_REHOME_PX re-anchor —
anchors at (X,Y). The two travel-from-the-clamp calls subtract the origin,
because the travel is a DELTA from the anchor and the target is absolute.

Default is +0+0 on every other station: identical behaviour, byte for byte.
No save item is touched, so a golden savestate is not orphaned.

--- a/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
+++ b/src/osd/modules/ctlsock/ctlsock.cpp
